│   ✅ Agent Finished                                                                                                                            │
│                                                                                                                                                │
│   Message:                                                                                                                                     │
│     I fixed the lost discriminator in `fastapi/dependencies/utils.py` so that `Annotated[Union[A, B], Field(discriminator=...), Body()]`       │
│ produces the same discriminated `oneOf` schema as `Body(discriminator=...)`.                                                                   │
│                                                                                                                                                │
│     **Root cause:** `analyze_param` builds the body field from the `Body()` FieldInfo, which has `discriminator=None`, so the `discriminator`  │
│ set on the separate `Field(...)` in the `Annotated` metadata was dropped from the OpenAPI schema. The fix copies a discriminator from any      │
│ other FieldInfo in the annotation when the chosen one has none.                                                                                │
│                                                                                                                                                │
│     **Verification:** A reproduction script showed the schema changing from `anyOf` to `oneOf` with the discriminator mapping, matching the    │
│ `Body(discriminator=...)` form. The existing `tests/test_union_body_discriminator.py` passes. I did not add regression tests, and I did not    │
│ confirm that the requests succeed in a run after the fix (the reproduction script only printed the schema after the fix).                      │
